A||N||6||3fifty||JC Whitney Simulated Rotors On A Fiero?||||5||
Z||000000||3fifty||08-07-2001||03:22 AM||||JC Whitney has the simulated cross drilled rotors for wheels for 5x4 1/2,5x4 3/4, & 5x5 bolt patterns. Does anyone know how close any of these are to the Fiero 5x100mm? Would either work or would you have to open the holes, or drill more?<P>Thanks,<BR>3fifty one day!!!!!!! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||08-07-2001||03:29 AM||||100mm is just over 4" Very close to 4 1/8"<BR>so all of those sizes are too far apart.<BR>Also "Simulated"!?! If it's the fake metal plate the sits behind the wheel, All they do is look fake and cause the brakes to run hotter. (Decreases air flow to cool rotors and brake pads)<BR>So my final question would be: "Why"???||||reg||1
Z||000002||3fifty||08-07-2001||03:41 AM||||Oreif,<BR>Since I have a body kit, I have custom 2" spacers to make the rear tires stick out.<BR>You can see how far the rotors are back in the wheel. I just thought that the simulated rotors would go between the wheel and spacer.<BR>The real rotor would stll be about 2 1/2" away from the simulator since the simulator would be on the outside of the spacer. ||||reg||10
Z||000003||artherd||08-07-2001||04:07 AM||||eek, holy bearing sideload, batman!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||08-07-2001||11:58 AM||||Artherd, not necessarily, if you had a set of wheels with alot of negative offset, you could have the spacers on it and it would put the mounting flange close to the center of the wheel. 1st-3rd gen Camaro guys do it all the time when they want to run newer Camaro wheels or even new Corvette rims on their cars.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||08-07-2001||12:28 PM||||the disk mounted that far outside from the rotor should be ok. If there rite on rotor like 'Kleanwheels' or similar they do overheat. I toasted my rear rotors in 1 week and Im ez on brakes. took them back off and new ones are fine after 3 years still.<P>I wont use adapters/spacers on mine. Thats reason I had wheels drilled to fit Fiero pattern, I drive hard and dont want to risk one breaking in the middle of a sweeper curve at 90 mph.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
